<title>MEXICO: Ahmsa to invest $90 mln in clean up.</title>
<headline>Ahmsa to invest $90 mln in clean up.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican steel company Altos Hornos SA (Ahmsa) plans to invest $90 million over the next eight years on environmental safeguards for its production process, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company added it has received the ISO-14001 environmental quality certification for its lamination process and steel oven number five.</p>
<p>--Daniel Perez Whitaker, Monterrey newsroom, +528 345-7617</p>
